# Query Patterns

## Timestamps
Always use UTC timestamps (suffix `Z` or `+00:00`). Convert any local time before querying.

## Index Pattern
Daily indices follow: `ppac-part3-YYYY.MM.DD`

## Field Names
- App name: `app.name` (e.g., LoginService)
- Use case: `entry.useCase` (e.g., forcelogoutPartner)
- Timestamp: `@timestamp`
- Message: `message`

## Search Logs
Use `es_post` with `/<index>/_search`:
```json
{
  "size": 5,
  "sort": [{"@timestamp": "desc"}],
  "query": {
    "bool": {
      "must": [
        {"match": {"app.name": "LoginService"}},
        {"range": {"@timestamp": {"gte": "2026-04-16T00:00:00Z", "lte": "2026-04-16T23:59:59Z"}}}
      ]
    }
  }
}
```

## Aggregations
For large datasets, always use aggregations instead of fetching documents. Set `"size": 0`:
```json
{
  "size": 0,
  "query": {"range": {"@timestamp": {"gte": "now-1d"}}},
  "aggs": {
    "by_app": {"terms": {"field": "app.name.keyword", "size": 20}}
  }
}
```

## Count Documents
Use `es_post` with `/<index>/_count` and a query body.

## Field Exploration
Use `es_query` with `/<index>/_mapping` to see available fields.

## Limits
- Default result size: 5
- Never fetch more than 50 documents at once
- Sort by `@timestamp: desc` unless asked otherwise
